<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump, Putin and Xi at one table, without Ukraine. What Moscow wants from the proposal and why Beijing might agree.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adbba5cccec070cdb6f477007df9c4ab48eb8efea553ea67ee8eab64a727427b</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-/a-79726190--eeff17927fb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Raids at far-right group's offices at European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f23606000fa39b1bdf9d596e7d21754e0bb68792fde794e385f1aebbc64a889</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631--002ed5188c2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities searched the Patriots for Europe's European Parliament offices in a long-running funding inquiry. The group says the charges pertain to its predecessor and there is "no legal continuity" between the two.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:230b31f633730bc3ce33e6be3acd9abc70bc091dc93eb2ff213105c01e234018</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia frees jailed American Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49c58864853fc7c1dc4aabc330950c3a3076260fdbcf9fb89ad19aec01237723</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452--b6488d619654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During talks between Vladimir Putin and Steve Witkoff, Putin announced that jailed American Stephen Hubbard had been released. The Kremlin also said Russia was "in principle" ready to resume trilateral talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK fighter jets to protect Saudi Arabia from Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b5afb121c01a07c6d28d2d7fe6da0b037ac065c258e6690d44f766ed13bda6</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T01:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467--d87226c03f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UK is sending military support to Saudi Arabia as Iran-aligned Houthi rebels launch repeated attacks on the kingdom.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal housing protests continue after police clear camps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d65df0a202df15a0d0801a12d59ad168a23a5a2f356c2af4259fffdc409ebbed</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904--9c24875c39a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators vow to continue their campaign to call for affordable housing in Portugal after police cleared tent camps and arrested at least 55 people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU plan for Arctic warily eyes influence of Russia, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4a96cc27b73b140042fee3fb9f3155d377fe4590619f269f0221fd35c557647</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219--7030ab283919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU unveiled its priorities in the Arctic as it vies with Russia, China and the US for influence. EU foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage undermine Arctic security.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89a72fa638fd2a23c47b7d983ac145b454a4ff3f08bc19a85a6bb126e4544b24</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Earth's sixth mass extinction event means for humans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e88f2293ecfe8d68ac58a288830bc332bcf5988e24bfe0798390ca14e6d9325</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410--0a12d110aea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human activity is driving plants and animals to extinction at an unprecedented rate. As countries meet in Armenia to discuss ways to reverse nature loss, DW reveals how declining biodiversity is already harming people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: Young voters blase about Glucksmann's Socialists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0c74ee2686bd5622851cbe7450eac76fac49e1d60e47145b2131f09dd65c8a0</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159--5c98176d41f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Raphael Glucksmann wants to lead France's Socialists to power without working with the left-populist Jean-Luc Melenchon, who is particularly popular with young voters. How can the center-left candidate win them over?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How reliant is Ukraine on the US-controlled Starlink internet service?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a60cbbdcdbd74ad98314e4977e46ae7dbfa722d7035a8d0e7032a4103192b16</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729--6217d664b01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kyiv keeps issuing warnings that the satellite internet system Starlink is being restricted in Ukraine. How dependent is the country on the system, and what would happen if it went down?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Populist Czech PM Babis goes empty-handed in Senate elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfe8a62913042f7c856eeef4baa0d39cbe7d96186f18d063bfa8e0aa0feb9e54</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934--95037aa1aa28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties still control the Czech Senate, in a major blow to Prime Minister Andrej Babis' and his governing coalition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50c47c3e659ddb5eab18df7630888a368e71e780288d2ae055a5744d628bc1bf</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703--c66cb23b1a91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy says Russia is trying to cut electricity and heating to civilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Protesters clash with police in nationwide protests, amid rising social polarization</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5640175577c2d632eaa49dbb43905446d15f255cf9aaf15a7e26fd6173eb4a10</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584--b410e6f9b726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Unrest broke out in parts of France as students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists took to the streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police arrested over 1,000 people amid chaotic scenes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e83cd9bbd88578a113392223db031e408ece08ea7455ca51317b3bc82aa341</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d22f518e7985b7ad375c0bacc21c4bf9f63e49038f3a6a34403f73440b6419f2</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39408d18bb364063cad853550dde1c9cd4c72bdfa244ecb452951a9b22018067</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95933806ef3eea31981883fdb4d0040d5a29fc6ac3418bc7ecf9e5bcc0b2dc46</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8593072d297a85eeab6099c9c09735a64a66b52e55f2e00595e651cca60f7dc6</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police raid the major pro-opposition Halk TV channel in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83d7b45f0713ae6517ed4fe5f7a0fad78b238370782e0c2fef59c06e1538a449</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673--402c2b295200.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of an important pro-opposition television station on Wednesdazy, the day that jailed Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu was set to start his defense against corruption charges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
